## 4. Recovery & Recommendations

### Recovery Strategy
1. Identify targeted file locations (`C:\Users\JohnDoe\Documents`)
2. Determine whether shadow copies or backups exist  
3. Remove persistence entries  
4. Restore clean system state or reimage workstation  
5. Restore user data from backups or carve deleted versions

### Recommendations
- Implement egress filtering to block unexpected outbound UDP on ports 80/443
- Enable endpoint logging (Sysmon, Windows Event Logging)
- Maintain offline backups resistant to ransomware
- Monitor registry Run keys for new persistence entries
- Use SIEM rules to detect beaconing patterns

---

## Conclusion
This project demonstrates—
- How to build a forensic workflow from network → disk → timeline  
- How to identify suspicious ransomware-style behavior  
- How to model recovery strategy without executing live malware  

The synthetic dataset approach kept the environment safe while still allowing realistic DFIR practice.
